This is the sample game for DUMB, a Doom-like 3D game engine.  You can
read more about DUMB at http://samba.anu.edu.au/dumb/.

Currently, there's only one level, a few rooms, no monsters, no exit.
Hopefully this will evolve into something better.  If it does, we'll
also have to find a real name for it, as "the DUMB game" sounds
rather... dumb.

This is the modernize branch, updated for current DUMB and autotools,
to go with the modernize branch of https://github.com/cadwal/dumb.  It
lives side by side with main, which keeps the original 0.13.1 sources
unchanged (also tagged original-0.13.1).  The first stage of this
work, the djgpp-modernize branch, is kept as the tag
djgpp-modernize-final.

To be able to build this, you must first install:
- DUMB 0.13.11 or later, with its tools ptcomp, wadtool, ppmtodumb and
  mkpnames (the modernize branch of https://github.com/cadwal/dumb;
  ppmtodumb needs the netpbm development library).  The .pt files
  use the current ptcomp syntax, so older DUMB versions won't work.
- netpbm
- GNU make.
- a C++ compiler, because we need the preprocessor.

So, if you just downloaded DUMB and this game, you'll first have to
install DUMB (or put its built ptcomp and tool directories in PATH).
Then come back and run "autoreconf -fi", configure and make.

The result is game.wad, an IWAD that needs nothing else.  Play it with
"xdumb -w game.wad" (or dosdumb.exe -w game.wad under DOS).

prebuilt/game.wad is a ready-made copy, for systems where the tools
above aren't available (e.g. building DUMB inside DOSBox-X).  Rebuild
it with "make" and copy game.wad there when the sources change.
Some textures are made by netpbm's ppmforge, which is random, so a
rebuild changes them; to keep the prebuilt art, copy over only the
lumps whose sources changed, e.g. after changing pt/ and lvl/:

  python3 tools/patch-lumps.py prebuilt/game.wad game.wad \
     prebuilt/game.wad PROTOS THINGS

E1M1 has starts for 4 players, so it can be played over the network
(DUMB's --dumb-master and --dumb-slave).  There is no player sprite
yet, so players can't see each other.
